{
  "id": "2SA.13",
  "number": "13",
  "bookId": "2SA",
  "reference": "2 Samuel 13",
  "verseCount": 39,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "13",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2SA 13"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "13",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now Absalom, David's son, had a beautiful sister, whose name was Tamar; and after a time Amnon, David's son, loved her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Amnon was so tormented that he made himself ill because of his sister Tamar; for she was a virgin, and it seemed impossible to Amnon to do anything to her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Amnon had a friend, whose name was Jonadab, the son of Shime-ah, David's brother; and Jonadab was a very crafty man. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said to him, “O son of the king, why are you so haggard morning after morning? Will you not tell me?” Amnon said to him, “I love Tamar, my brother Absalom's sister.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jonadab said to him, “Lie down on your bed, and pretend to be ill; and when your father comes to see you, say to him, ‘Let my sister Tamar come and give me bread to eat, and prepare the food in my sight, that I may see it, and eat it from her hand.’ ” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Amnon lay down, and pretended to be ill; and when the king came to see him, Amnon said to the king, “Pray let my sister Tamar come and make a couple of cakes in my sight, that I may eat from her hand.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then David sent home to Tamar, saying, “Go to your brother Amnon's house, and prepare food for him.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Tamar went to her brother Amnon's house, where he was lying down. And she took dough, and kneaded it, and made cakes in his sight, and baked the cakes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And she took the pan and emptied it out before him, but he refused to eat. And Amnon said, “Send out every one from me.” So every one went out from him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Amnon said to Tamar, “Bring the food into the chamber, that I may eat from your hand.” And Tamar took the cakes she had made, and brought them into the chamber to Amnon her brother. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But when she brought them near him to eat, he took hold of her, and said to her, “Come, lie with me, my sister.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "She answered him, “No, my brother, do not force me; for such a thing is not done in Israel; do not do this wanton folly. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As for me, where could I carry my shame? And as for you, you would be as one of the wanton fools in Israel. Now therefore, I pray you, speak to the king; for he will not withhold me from you.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But he would not listen to her; and being stronger than she, he forced her, and lay with her.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Amnon hated her with very great hatred; so that the hatred with which he hated her was greater than the love with which he had loved her. And Amnon said to her, “Arise, be gone.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But she said to him, “No, my brother; for this wrong in sending me away is greater than the other which you did to me.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13.16",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Cn Compare Gk Vg: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "No, for this great wrong in sending me away is (worse) than the other which you did to me",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " But he would not listen to her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He called the young man who served him and said, “Put this woman out of my presence, and bolt the door after her.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now she was wearing a long robe with sleeves; for thus were the virgin daughters of the king clad of old.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13.18",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Cn: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "clad in robes",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " So his servant put her out, and bolted the door after her. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Tamar put ashes on her head, and rent the long robe which she wore; and she laid her hand on her head, and went away, crying aloud as she went.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And her brother Absalom said to her, “Has Amnon your brother been with you? Now hold your peace, my sister; he is your brother; do not take this to heart.” So Tamar dwelt, a desolate woman, in her brother Absalom's house. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When King David heard of all these things, he was very angry. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Absalom spoke to Amnon neither good nor bad; for Absalom hated Amnon, because he had forced his sister Tamar.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After two full years Absalom had sheepshearers at Baal-hazor, which is near Ephraim, and Absalom invited all the king's sons. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Absalom came to the king, and said, “Behold, your servant has sheepshearers; pray let the king and his servants go with your servant.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But the king said to Absalom, “No, my son, let us not all go, lest we be burdensome to you.” He pressed him, but he would not go but gave him his blessing. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Absalom said, “If not, pray let my brother Amnon go with us.” And the king said to him, “Why should he go with you?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Absalom pressed him until he let Amnon and all the king's sons go with him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Absalom commanded his servants, “Mark when Amnon's heart is merry with wine, and when I say to you, ‘Strike Amnon,’ then kill him. Fear not; have I not commanded you? Be courageous and be valiant.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So the servants of Absalom did to Amnon as Absalom had commanded. Then all the king's sons arose, and each mounted his mule and fled.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.29"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "While they were on the way, tidings came to David, “Absalom has slain all the king's sons, and not one of them is left.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the king arose, and rent his garments, and lay on the earth; and all his servants who were standing by rent their garments. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Jonadab the son of Shime-ah, David's brother, said, “Let not my lord suppose that they have killed all the young men the king's sons, for Amnon alone is dead, for by the command of Absalom this has been determined from the day he forced his sister Tamar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now therefore let not my lord the king so take it to heart as to suppose that all the king's sons are dead; for Amnon alone is dead.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.33"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Absalom fled. And the young man who kept the watch lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold, many people were coming from the Horonaim road",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13.34",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Cn Compare Gk: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the road behind him",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " by the side of the mountain. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Jonadab said to the king, “Behold, the king's sons have come; as your servant said, so it has come about.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And as soon as he had finished speaking, behold, the king's sons came, and lifted up their voice and wept; and the king also and all his servants wept very bitterly.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.36"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Absalom fled, and went to Talmai the son of Ammihud, king of Geshur. And David mourned for his son day after day. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.37"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "38",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:38"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "38",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So Absalom fled, and went to Geshur, and was there three years. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "39",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 13:39"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "39",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the spirit",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.39",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.39"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13.39",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "David",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " of the king longed to go forth to Absalom; for he was comforted about Amnon, seeing he was dead.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.13.39",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.13.39"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
